                                    <h2><span class="shaft"><img id="1146-0" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_o.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Omnidirectional" title="Omnidirectional" ><img id="1146-1" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_c.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Cardioid" title="Cardioid" ><img id="1146-2" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_sc.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Supercardioid" title="Supercardioid" ><img id="1146-3" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_wc.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Wide Cardioid" title="Wide Cardioid" ></span>Schoeps Mikrofone CMC 5</h2>
                    
                    <h2 class="sub">                    Detachable-Capsule Pencil Condenser Microphone</h2>
                    <p>The CMC 5 is a transformerless, balanced head amplifier for the Schoeps &#8220;Colette&#8221; series of modular microphones. Although a newer version has been released (see the CMC 6), the CMC 5 remains in production.</p><p>Any of 20 different capsules can be used with the CMC head amps, including both end- and side-address versions of most polar patterns. Special-purpose capsules for speech, for distant miking, and for very close miking are available. </p><p><em>How is the CMC 5 different from the CMC 6?</em></p><p>These two head amps differ in their powering modes and the shape of their built-in high-pass filters.</p><p>The CMC 5 required +48V phantom power, but runs at a low 4mA current draw. The CMC 6 has an additional powering mode (+12V, 8mA) with an internal detection and switching circuit.</p><p>The CMC 5 has a fixed low-frequency filter, intended to reduce rumble and mechanical noise. It is a -6dB/octave slope, rolling off below 30Hz. In contrast, the CMC 6 filter is twice as steep, but begins at a lower frequency.</p><p>This head amp is produced in two finishes: matte grey and satin nickel. It can be special-ordered with a different low-frequency filter slope or cutoff for special applications.<p>The <a href="//recordinghacks.com/microphones/Schoeps/CMC-5">Schoeps Mikrofone CMC 5</a> is also known as: CMC-5U.</p>
